            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0562" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6327: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-29T17:00:00+02:00">October 29, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>852. I called this afternoon on the Greek Minister to express indignation at the
                    act of aggression to which his country has been subjected.</p>
                <p>He had no news of the day’s developments nor of the attitude which either Turkey
                    or Bulgaria may assume. The Foreign Office likewise has no news.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
